{
 "MISSION": "OMLDCT02",
 "SECTION": "frozen forbidden-seed set",
 "GENERATED_UTC": "2026-08-25T22:15:56.514840+00:00",
 "GENERATOR": "OMLDCT02/code/omldct02_forbidden_seeds.py",
 "WHY_THIS_IS_A_SEPARATE_FROZEN_STEP": "OMLDCT02 \u2014 the frozen forbidden-seed set.\n\nThe first version of the seed generator harvested the forbidden set from the repository at\ngeneration time. It was NOT reproducible, and the reason is worth recording: once the generator had\nwritten OMLDCT02_SEED_MANIFEST.json, that file sat in the repository with its own seeds under keys\ncontaining the word 'seed', so the next run treated OMLDCT02's own seeds as forbidden and produced a\ncompletely different list. A self-poisoning harvest.\n\nCaught before C1, and fixed structurally rather than patched: the harvest is now its own committed\nstep producing its own frozen artefact, the harvest excludes OMLDCT02's own directory by rule, and\nthe seed generator reads the frozen file instead of re-scanning. Both steps are then idempotent.",
 "RULE": "a deliberate superset. Every integer in [0, 2**32) under any key containing 'seed' in any JSON in the repository, every _s<digits> or seed<digits> token in any filename in the repository, and every such token in every .npz filename on the Windows device. Over-excluding costs nothing; under-excluding would let OMLDCT02 reuse a seed whose outcome is already known somewhere in the programme.",
 "EXCLUDED_SUBTREES": [
  "/.git",
  "/OMLDCT02"
 ],
 "EXCLUSION_RULE": "the harvest covers everything the programme ran BEFORE OMLDCT02, so OMLDCT02's own subtree is excluded by rule. Including it would make the harvest depend on its own output, which is exactly the defect this file was written to remove.",
